.TH MORIA 1 "2026-09-10" "moria 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
moria \- find and unpack files stored inside firmware
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moria
.RI [ options ]
.I <file|dir>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B moria
finds known file types stored inside firmware and other device-software files.
This includes file systems, packaged files, startup programs, programs,
compressed data, and media. For each match, it shows the starting byte and how
strongly the file contents support the match. With
.B \-\-extract
it can unpack supported file systems, archives, and firmware packages directly,
without \fBsudo\fR. Supported file systems include SquashFS, ext2/3/4, F2FS,
JFFS2, UBIFS, romfs, YAFFS2, cramfs, FAT, exFAT, NTFS, HFS+, XFS, btrfs,
EROFS, and ISO 9660. It also unpacks ZIP, tar, and cpio archives; U-Boot uImage
and FIT packages; and RAE Systems/Honeywell RFP firmware packages. Other known
formats are still named and located so another program can handle them.
.PP
Output is easy to read by default. A single file shows a tree of matches,
including files found inside other files, followed by totals. A folder shows
counts by file type and groups important matches by folder. Pass
.BR \-j / \-\-json
to return one structured JSON object for other programs and AI tools.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I <file|dir>
A file to check, or a folder whose files should be checked.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Return JSON instead of the normal easy-to-read view. Use this when another
program or AI tool will read the results.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-all
Show matches found inside larger file systems and packages. moria normally
hides internal compressed pieces that are already handled when the larger file
system is unpacked. This keeps the report and output folders from filling with
duplicate pieces. \fB\-A\fR shows and unpacks those pieces too.
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-entropy
Measure how random the unknown parts of a file look. This check is off by
default. The JSON result adds an \fBunidentified_regions\fR list with each part's
starting byte, size, and entropy score. Entropy is a 0-to-8 measure; a high score
can mean that data is encrypted or compressed. moria does not warn about
compressed data that belongs to a file system it already recognized.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List the names and sizes of files inside tar, cpio, or ZIP archives without
unpacking them.
.SS Extract
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-extract
Unpack supported file systems, archives, Android images, U-Boot packages, and
RAE Systems/Honeywell RFP firmware packages into
.IR file .extracted/
(one folder for each match, named
.IR 0x<starting-byte>\-<type> ).
moria also checks the files it unpacks and continues through supported files
found inside them.
Use
.BR \-\-depth ", " \-\-max\-files ", and " \-\-max\-bytes
to limit this work. Reading ext2/3/4 file systems does not change them and
needs no \fBsudo\fR. Takes one file, not a folder.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-outdir " " \fIdir\fR
Write unpacked or copied files to
.I dir
instead of the default
.IR file .extracted/ .
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " N"
Number of file-within-a-file levels to unpack (default 8).
.B \-\-depth 1
unpacks only matches in the original file.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-files " N"
Stop after writing
.I N
files in total (default 500000). The \fBmanifest.json\fR index is marked
.IR capped .
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-bytes " N"
Stop after writing
.I N
bytes in total (default 4294967296, or 4 GiB). The \fBmanifest.json\fR index is marked
.IR capped .
moria also stops unpacking any item larger than 10 MiB when it expands to more
than 1,000 times its stored size.
.SS Carve
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-carve
Copy the exact bytes for each match, plus unknown gaps between matches, to
.IR file .carved/
as
.IR <starting-byte> \- <type> .bin
files. This operation is called carving. It does not try to understand the
copied data. Use it when
.B \-\-extract
cannot rebuild a file system because the data is scrambled, damaged, or not yet
supported. The copied bytes can then be checked by hand or given to another
program. An index named
.I manifest.json
records each copied part's starting byte, size, and type. This option works
separately from
.BR \-\-extract "; when both are given, carve writes to a sibling"
.IR file .carved/
folder. By default, gaps smaller than 1 KiB are not copied because they are
usually unused space;
.B \-A
copies every gap. Obeys
.B \-C
and
.BR \-\-max\-bytes .
Takes a single file, not a folder.
.SS More file types
.TP
.B \-\-broad
Also use about 2,500 general file-recognition rules created from file(1)'s
Magdir database.
.SS Settings
.TP
.BI \-\-sigs " dir"
Use file-recognition rules from a specific folder instead of the built-in rules.
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " N"
Number of files to check at the same time during folder checks. The default is
the number of processor cores, up to 16.
.SS Information
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Could not read a file or load any file-recognition rules.
.TP
.B 2
The command is incomplete or includes an unknown option.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MORIA_SIGDIR
Uses file-recognition rules from this folder (same effect as \fB\-\-sigs\fR).
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
If set, \fBmoria\fR looks for signatures under \fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/moria\fR (else
\fB~/.local/share/moria\fR) as part of its search path.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables bold section headers in \fB\-\-help\fR output.
.SH FILES
When no \fB\-\-sigs\fR or \fBMORIA_SIGDIR\fR is given, moria looks for
recognition rules beside the program (\fB<exe>/../signatures\fR and
\fB<exe>/../share/moria/\fR), then in \fB~/.local/share/moria\fR, then in
\fB/usr/local/share/moria\fR and \fB/usr/share/moria\fR. \fBcmake \-\-install\fR
places the rules in \fB<prefix>/share/moria/\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check one file and show easy-to-read results:
.B moria firmware.bin
.TP
Check one file and return JSON for another program:
.B moria \-j firmware.bin
.TP
Unpack its file systems:
.B moria \-e firmware.bin
.TP
Copy exact byte ranges to separate files:
.B moria \-c firmware.bin
.TP
List archive contents without unpacking:
.B moria \-\-list update.tar
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR file (1),
.BR binwalk (1)
.PP
Full documentation: README.md
